{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543502-who-loves-the-setting-but-not-either-system","id":1543502,"title":"Who Loves the Setting But Not Either System?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-10T01:13:30-07:00","id":1543502,"title":"Who Loves the Setting But Not Either System?","content":"Are there folks here who are like that? Which system do you use as an alternative?<br /> Is anyone else thinking of looking at Curseborne as a base, even if only experimentally?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T16:39:02-07:00","id":1543559,"title":"","content":"I'm using v20 system but i completed it with some rules i found in v5 and in 2 other game, mostly to reduce the dice rolls in combat.<br /> Other that that i use a lot of houserule to adapt the game to our way of playing and to fit our story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T18:03:44-07:00","id":1543562,"title":"","content":"Never been a big fan of the Storyteller system. Like, it works and it gets the job done, but it's not a system I'd specifically choose to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T18:34:18-07:00","id":1543564,"title":"","content":"I have some plans to translate WoD to both D&amp;D (at least 3.5 edition) and Mutants &amp; Masterminds 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> While the D&amp;D version has more specific purposes, the M&amp;M one is precisely to see if it works better as a system.<br /> <br /> Overall I don't have the same urgency with CoD. I think it does the job well enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T20:35:42-07:00","id":1543568,"title":"","content":"The Storyteller System is great for its intended purpose, which is to be explained in a couple of sentences and intuitively used. This in turn allows people to pick up the game very quickly compared to other systems which require a lot of reading and memorization of granular mechanics. As such, there is generally little need to convert the entire setting to a different mechanics setup.<br /> <br /> But I will agree that the Storyteller System has holes in it, so rather than a full conversion I tend to use &quot;chunks&quot; of other systems to patch the areas where it falls down. Usually this means I use a different system to run sub-game sections, such as running a Warhammer Fantasy or Warhammer 40K minis game with custom point costs to simulate battles and sieges. This is especially useful when you have PCs which are minion heavy builds or rely extensively on using Backgrounds from a distance rather than fighting in person. Once the mini's game is resolved, I take the results and use that outcome as the baseline for the next section of normal Storyteller System use.<br /> <br /> VtM starts as a street level game about a coterie doing their best &quot;The Lost Boys&quot; impression, but after a certain amount of XP is gained it more or less becomes almost a Real Time Strategy game where you use influence and minions to achieve your goals rather than directly punching things. But the Storyteller System doesn't really have rules for that transition beyond a lot of hand waving and abstraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T07:57:22-07:00","id":1543580,"title":"","content":"For a long time, I basically ran a simplified version where you aimed for a fixed target number of 6+. 1s cancelled successes and 10s counted twice. Specialisations let you re-roll one die (usually a 1, since that could net you two successes if you were lucky). Even one success was a win, but it might be a partial success in tricky situations.<br /> <br /> Combat was always the most involved part. I think everyone ignored the &quot;declare in reverse order&quot; thing anyway, and probably used the same initiative across subsequent rounds.<br /> <br /> We were never that bothered by all the rolling for attack/damage/soak (no one ever used the defensive actions, preferring to save up their turn for their own attack), but we did try leaving the damage and soak unrolled and just subtracting the latter from the former. It works, so long as you apply a minimum damage for lethal and aggravated attacks. But it can also be pretty devastating for those attacks that get through. Or you can roll one and take half for the other.<br /> <br /> CofD2e works much better, so you can just use those rules (or the Exalted/Trinity ones) if it makes more sense. I'll be stealing what I like from Curseborne, probably, but I don't think I'll ever be able to love it as much as Classic WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T20:07:02-07:00","id":1543818,"title":"","content":"Cyberpunk: 2020's <i>Night's Edge</i> is a good alternative. But if I want to play a vampire-game, I get out my Masquerade-book and use the ST-system. I've used Night's Edge when the players either got tired of V:tM, or, they got too good at vampire and I wanted to present a more lethal-system. It's also very good at Ricean-games, if you read her novels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T20:58:51-07:00","id":1543826,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m looking forward to the new WoD5 releases advertised at Renegade Con last Friday. In Memoriam for V5, Apostates for H5 and Wyrmtide for W5 all look really good. I\u2019m thinking I may have judged WoD5 a little too harshly.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this isn\u2019t in the right place. I wasn\u2019t sure which question it fit under.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 10-15-2024, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T22:45:38-07:00","id":1543835,"title":"","content":"There's GURPS VtM, WtA and MtAs, but that system isn't to everyone's taste, either. You could use the VtR/VtM conversion guide, but the system is still pretty similar to Storyteller (though far more refined in my opinion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19862-jadeite","name":"jadeite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T04:23:04-07:00","id":1544085,"title":"","content":"I actually like the sustem 'as is' but I'll explain why with a couple of points.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543502-who-loves-the-setting-but-not-either-system?p=1543580#post1543580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think everyone ignored the &quot;declare in reverse order&quot; thing anyway, and probably used the same initiative across subsequent rounds.<br /> <br /> We were never that bothered by all the rolling for attack/damage/soak (no one ever used the defensive actions, preferring to save up their turn for their own attack)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a fairly common option taken by many groups but there are some potential pitfalls.<br /> <br /> If your init is the same across multiple turns then that causes the 'no-one ever used defensive actions' problem because you have no choice but to risk being hit in order to attack.<br /> <br /> Frome one point of view WoD system is designed for _duelling_ i.e. 1v1 combat. Which is why you need to roll init each round and why you only get a choice of attacking or defending and why the reverse init declare is important.<br /> <br /> In the situation where A is figting B and A wins init then B has to choose between attacking and leaving themselves open, or defending but skipping an attack, because they don't know what A will do. When the situation reverse in subsequent turns A has to decide. 1v1 this is quite fast to resolve and is pretty good for dramatic tension.<br /> <br /> The problem is that this is very slow when it's not 1v1 which is why so many compromises and house rules are created.<br /> <br /> My 'house rule' is that the ST goes round the table and resolves combat as a series of 1v1 duels. This does demand a certain amount of 'fixing' by the ST to provide suitable opponents but is overal, in my opinion, a better solution.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other 'misconception' is that WoD is actually a _superhero_ system... obvioulsy one that leans heavily into the 'dark and gritty' theme but the system itself is all about people with fantasical, superhuman powers. The dice system also tends towards success for the characters, pools as low as three dice regularly succeed whereas in other systems low skilled characters tend to fail most of the time. Once you understand this then being an ST is remarkably easier - you expect the players to succeed which means you can guide the story more reliably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 10-17-2024, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T13:33:09-07:00","id":1544132,"title":"","content":"I'm running CoD2E (Mummy the Curse) at the moment and like it very much. If I run a VDA20 or V20 game in the future, I'll be likely to run it with CoD2E rules. Many things are already written for VtR, I just need to &quot;translate&quot; some Disciplines and adjust some mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T20:07:59-07:00","id":1544336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543502-who-loves-the-setting-but-not-either-system?p=1544132#post1544132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running CoD2E (Mummy the Curse) at the moment and like it very much. If I run a VDA20 or V20 game in the future, I'll be likely to run it with CoD2E rules. Many things are already written for VtR, I just need to &quot;translate&quot; some Disciplines and adjust some mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Masquerade-days, I often thought that other supernaturals, should be run in the game-system your running; ie, Werewolves should use disciplines, vampires in WW: tA should have gifts, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T23:40:44-07:00","id":1544343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543502-who-loves-the-setting-but-not-either-system?p=1544336#post1544336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Masquerade-days, I often thought that other supernaturals, should be run in the game-system your running; ie, Werewolves should use disciplines, vampires in WW: tA should have gifts, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered the same, but I think it's because those games were similar but not actually written to be compatible, causing multiple issues when using the powers of one in a game of the other. And even on mundane things like maneuvers in combat there were contradictions, like the same maneuver working differently in VtM and WtA, but not just because of obvious difference between vampires and werewolves: humans in a VtM game would be using that same maneuver as written in VtM, while humans in WtA would use it as written in VtM.<br /> <br /> With CoD2 there is much less of that because all the splats use the same mundane system and their supernatural features are generally compatible and comparable. Of course, some are stronger than others by design (mummies trash vampires, for example), but they are still written to operate in the same world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T03:44:52-08:00","id":1545453,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for some interesting rules you can check Warhammer 40k Wrath &amp; Glory, the system is extremely similar to V5 (basically they use d6 instead of d10 and have a different approach to combat). Maybe you'll find something usefull for your game inside this book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}